1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:27,750
Imagine inheriting a route migration.

2
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:49,875
You can see three saved conversations
in Chronicle, but which change landed,

3
00:00:49,875 --> 00:01:06,500
which check passed, and what should you
do next?

4
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,875
Lab zero gives us eight minutes to
establish a baseline.

5
00:01:09,875 --> 00:01:14,833
Chronicle already parses two session
formats and reconstructs file changes.

6
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:19,833
A passing local suite gives us
something to compare against after each

7
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:20,250
change.

8
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:23,875
Lab one spends seventeen minutes on
ownership.

9
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:29,792
A single public orchestrator reads,
searches, delegates and tracks a

10
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:30,375
checklist.

11
00:01:30,375 --> 00:01:35,333
It cannot edit the application, so a
request has to cross an explicit

12
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:36,875
boundary to the developer.

13
00:01:36,875 --> 00:01:38,750
The tester can run the code.

14
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:41,792
The security reviewer can only read and
search.

15
00:01:41,792 --> 00:01:44,667
Documentation explains the contract.

16
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:50,750
If a test fails or the reviewer finds a
serious leak, the lead sends the change

17
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:52,667
back rather than declaring victory.

18
00:01:52,667 --> 00:01:56,500
Lab two gives the team fifteen minutes
to encode its methods.

19
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:01,625
The developer's zero-package skill
teaches an atomic write: build a

20
00:02:01,625 --> 00:02:07,208
temporary file and rename it, so a
partial write never becomes the saved

21
00:02:07,208 --> 00:02:07,625
configuration.

22
00:02:07,625 --> 00:02:13,500
The tester's playbook replaces identity
and model servers with loopback mocks.

23
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:56,917
Security checks what can leave the
process.

24
00:02:56,917 --> 00:03:00,417
Documentation specifies the handoff
format.

25
00:03:00,417 --> 00:03:05,250
Each skill name matches its folder and
is attached to the matching role.

26
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:08,458
Lab three takes fifteen minutes.

27
00:03:08,458 --> 00:03:14,958
The dialog collects the tenant, client,
secret, endpoint and agent name.

28
00:03:14,958 --> 00:03:20,667
The browser may learn that a secret is
saved, but must not retrieve its value

29
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:22,167
from the configuration API.

30
00:03:22,167 --> 00:03:27,083
The local server asks Entra for a
token, then uses it for a Foundry

31
00:03:27,083 --> 00:03:27,792
Responses request.

32
00:03:27,792 --> 00:03:32,000
A READY reply proves more than saving
the settings.

33
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,792
Separate authentication and agent
timings help locate a failure without

34
00:03:36,792 --> 00:03:37,750
printing credentials.

35
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:43,083
Lab four has eighteen minutes to turn a
selected session into portable

36
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:43,542
Markdown.

37
00:03:43,542 --> 00:03:46,875
The button lives next to Read full
session.

38
00:03:46,875 --> 00:03:51,875
The input is a read-only source; the
new summary belongs in a separate

39
00:03:51,875 --> 00:03:52,583
output folder.

40
00:03:52,583 --> 00:05:17,417
Build a chronological digest of
prompts, recorded decisions, tools and

41
00:05:17,417 --> 00:05:25,917
edits.

42
00:05:25,917 --> 00:05:29,333
Replace machine paths with
workspace-relative ones.

43
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:34,667
A short digest goes straight to
synthesis; a long one becomes bounded

44
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:38,250
chunks whose individual digests feed
the final pass.

45
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:42,333
The progress dialog reports phases, not
just a spinner.

46
00:05:42,333 --> 00:05:54,792
Inspect a redacted operation log for
the job history.

47
00:05:54,792 --> 00:06:11,500
Then read the Markdown as the next
developer: can you name a tested result

48
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:17,458
and the next unfinished task?

49
00:06:17,458 --> 00:06:22,125
Lab five closes with seventeen minutes
on release evidence.

50
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:25,000
A pure Node renderer produces the icon.

51
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:39,583
Test its URL, media type and signature.

52
00:06:39,583 --> 00:06:44,417
A visible browser tab icon alone could
be an old cached copy.

53
00:06:44,417 --> 00:06:49,667
The optional desktop wrapper adds a
sandboxed window, a separate server

54
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:52,042
process and narrow native pickers.

55
00:06:52,042 --> 00:06:54,083
Inspect it without running it.

56
00:06:54,083 --> 00:06:58,875
Our deliverable is still the browser
app, and the next developer gets a

57
00:06:58,875 --> 00:07:01,833
portable plan instead of somebody
else's environment.
